The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
for (i = 0; i < PTE_PREFETCH_NUM; i++, spte++) {
    if (is_shadow_present_pte(*spte) || spte == sptep) {
        if (!start)
            continue;
        ...
    } else if (!start)
        start = spte;
}
```
Reason:
The loop only handles the case for preceding SPTEs that are present, and if all preceding SPTEs are not present, it fails to prefetch any trailing SPTEs for GFNs that follow the faulting GFN. This results in missed prefetching of necessary SPTEs, leading to an increased number of guest page faults.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (start)
    direct_pte_prefetch_many(vcpu, sp, start, spte);
```
Reason:
This addition ensures that if there are any trailing SPTEs to prefetch (indicated by `start` being non-null), a final call to `direct_pte_prefetch_many()` is made to prefetch those SPTEs, thus addressing the issue of missed prefetching and reducing the number of guest page faults.

